  "version": 4,
  "description": "Finite store of the known non-credential occurrences accepted by the no-hardcoded-secrets check. Acceptance requires an exact match on ALL of file + kind + sha256 of the exact regex match substring + location: the line number, and for parsed JSON key/value hits the JSON pointer. Pointers are templates — a secret-shaped property-name segment is stored as the stable placeholder \"<key>\" so no raw key is ever written here; text hits carry a null pointer. Moving an occurrence within the same file fails. A disposition for a file that IS present but no longer matches (changed or removed occurrence) is stale and fails. A disposition whose file is ABSENT from the scanned tree (for example the untracked workstreams evidence files on a clean CI checkout) is inert, matching the replaced git-grep gate's verdict on a file that is not there: it is printed as an explicit NOTE line, never silent, but does not fail the run. Matched values are never stored here — only their digests. Every entry names in \"source\" the adjudication receipt(s) it derives from, resolved relative to the mini-pack-qa-remediation phase of the bossfang-uar-architecture planning workstream. Re-adjudication 2026-10-08: docker/AGENTS.md entries re-bound from line 28 to line 35 after the merged main doc rewrite; occurrence digests unchanged; still 24 finite dispositions.",
